---
// Not in 03-PAGE-SPECS, but 02-ARCHITECTURE/robots.txt already disallows /thank-you/,
// so the kit assumes it exists. noindex as well as disallowed: robots.txt stops crawling,
// not indexing from an external link.
//
// This is where the form's conversion event fires — 08-LAUNCH/01-pre-launch-checklist.md:
// "Conversion tracking on the form, not on the page view."
import UtilityLayout from '../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro';
import { SITE, token } from '../../lib/site.js';
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Request received — Plainly"
  description="Your valuation request has been received. What happens next, when the call comes and when the written report arrives: 15 minutes and 24 hours respectively."
  noindex={true}
  h1="Request received"
>
  <p class="answer">
    Your request has gone to the licensed partner who produces the valuation. Expect a call
    within 15 minutes during operating hours, and the written report by email within 24 hours.
  </p>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>A call to confirm the building, the unit size and whether it is tenanted</li>
    <li>Comparable transactions pulled for your building from Land Department records</li>
    <li>A written report by email within 24 hours, listing every transaction it used</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>If you do not hear back</h2>
  <p>
    Call <span class="pending">{token(SITE.phone, 'PHONE')}</span> directly. A request that
    goes unanswered is a fault at this end, not a queue.
  </p>

  <h2>While you wait</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/property-valuation-dubai/how-it-works/">How the valuation is produced</a> —
      the three methods and what each one is for
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/property-valuation-dubai/golden-visa/">The golden visa threshold</a> — if AED
      2 million is the number you care about
    </li>
  </ul>
</UtilityLayout>
